@startuml Sequence_5
hide footbox
title Scenario 5: Enemy Turn — Goblin Is Stunned, Skips Turn

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor       "User"                         as User
boundary    "ArenaBattleScreen"            as Screen
control     "GameApp\n<<ActionCallbacks>>" as App
control     "BattleEngine"                 as Engine
entity      "Goblin\n<<Enemy>>"            as Goblin
entity      "StunEffect\n<<StatusEffect>>" as Stun
entity      "GameState\n<<Static>>"        as State

note over User, State
  This is the enemy phase of the same executePlayerTurn() call as Scenario 4.
  Warrior (SPD=30) already used Shield Bash — StunEffect on Goblin (remainingTurns=2).
  Now: Goblin (SPD=25) tries to act but cannot.
end note

' ── User Input (same round as Scenario 4) ──────────────────────
User -> Screen : clicks "Special Skill" button
note right of User
  Same user action that triggered Scenario 4.
  Shown here for continuity — enemy phase
  occurs in the same executePlayerTurn() call.
end note

Screen -> App : callbacks.onSpecialSkill(targetIndex)
App -> Engine : executePlayerTurn(choice=4, targetIndex, null, 1.0)
note right of App : choice=4 → Shield Bash branch (Scenario 4)

note over Engine
  Warrior phase: Shield Bash ran, StunEffect applied to Goblin.
  (See Scenario 4 for player phase detail.)
  Now processing: Goblin (instanceof Enemy).
end note

' ── Goblin Phase — Stunned ─────────────────────────────────────
Engine -> Goblin : beginTurn()
note over Goblin
  Iterates activeEffects → finds StunEffect.
  Calls StunEffect.onTurnStart(goblin).
end note
Goblin -> Stun : onTurnStart(goblin)
note over Stun
  remainingTurns > 0
  remainingTurns-- (2 → 1)
  returns true → skip this turn
end note
Stun --> Goblin : true (skip turn)

note over Goblin
  canAct = false.
  StunEffect.isExpired()? turns=1 → no, stays active.
  returns false.
end note
Goblin --> Engine : false (cannot act)

note over Engine
  enemy.beginTurn() == false.
  Enemy AI strategy is NOT executed.
  No attack TurnFrame is added for Goblin.
end note

Engine -> Engine : sweepDeadEnemies()
note over Engine : Goblin hp > 0 — nothing removed.

' ── End of Round ───────────────────────────────────────────────
Engine -> State : checkEndCondition()
State --> Engine : 0 (continue)
Engine -> Engine : endRound()
note right of Engine
  round++
  warrior.decrementCooldownAfterTurn() → cooldown: 3→2
  GameState.newTurnOrder() — Goblin still alive with StunEffect (turns=1)
end note
Engine --> App : 0 (continue)

' ── Render Result ──────────────────────────────────────────────
App -> Engine : drainTurnFrames()
Engine --> App : [TurnFrame("Warrior casts Shield Bash.", dmg=25)]\nnote: no Goblin attack frame — Goblin was stunned
App -> Screen : render(ArenaViewState)
Screen --> User : updated battle screen\n(Goblin did not attack — Stun icon remains)

@enduml
